# Copy to booking-engine/.env and fill in. Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed vars.

# Base URL of the PMS API. This is where /book gets its rooms, rates,
# occupancy limits, currency and availability — with it set, nothing on the
# booking page is authored on the site. Leave it unset to build a standalone
# site that prices from bundled placeholders and cannot take a booking, which
# is what the GitHub Pages build does.
#
# The API's CORS_ORIGIN must list this site's origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173).
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Only needed when the PMS runs more than one property — with one, the public
# endpoints answer for it without being asked. Use the property's code as it
# appears in the PMS (e.g. MELLOW).
# VITE_PROPERTY_CODE=

# The same thing by id, for a deployment that would rather pin the id than the
# code. Set one or the other, not both.
# VITE_PROPERTY_ID=

# There is deliberately no API token here.
#
# The site books through the public endpoint only. It posts the guest's
# selection and the PMS resolves the room type, the rate plan and the price
# itself. An earlier build could instead be given VITE_API_TOKEN plus hard-coded
# room-type and rate-plan ids and post to the private /api/reservations — that
# path is gone. It duplicated pricing logic in the browser, and a token in a
# browser bundle is readable by everyone who opens the page.
#
# A booking taken here arrives in the PMS awaiting confirmation: it holds no
# inventory and cannot be checked in until somebody at the property accepts it
# and picks the room or beds.
